extends Node

func define_texts():
	var t = {}
	t['ManualDefault'] = "Select A Topic..."
	t['ManualEx0'] = "You can just start a new game right now! Make sure that you have the tutorial level enabled. All the basics will be explained within the first few fights. Just listen to the dialogue and read the text. But if you insist on reading... Sonny is a turn based fighting game. You choose what move your character makes in his turn by first selecting WHO you want to make a move on, and then you can choose WHAT you want to do to that target. For example, if you want to attack an enemy, you click on the enemy first, then you can choose to attack him. If you want to heal a team mate, select that character and you will be able to choose a move to use on him. You may only have 8 moves 'equipped' in any fight, and you configure this from your Abilities menu. Some moves can be equipped more than once, so that you can use it more often."
	t['ManualEx1'] = "They just indicate the element that the ability is classified as: [color=red]Physical[/color], [color=pink]Cosmic[/color], [color=orange]Fire[/color], [color=lightblue]Ice[/color], [color=yellow]Lightning[/color], [color=darkbrown]Earth[/color], [color=purple]Shadow[/color], and [color=darkgreen]Poison[/color]."
	t['ManualEx2'] = "During battle, you can cannot directly control the actions of your team mates, but you can tell them how to behave. You can also equip your team mates with items and weapons, by going into the inventory screen."
	t['ManualEx3'] = "Strength and Instinct are just co-efficients for your abilities. Speed is also a co-efficient, but to only a few abilities. Speed also increases your critical strike chance and dodge/accuracy. Vitality increases your Health. Piercing increases critical strike chance, and Defense decreases damage taken."
	t['ManualEx4'] = "It's mainly about the Strategy and Abilities that you use. Observe the enemy carefully, and look into your entire Ability tree to find ways to beat them. If you need more help, then try visiting the Sonny forums on ArmorGames for guides and walkthroughs."
	return t
